    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Zack Gelof** (66.86) leads the charge as our premier offensive anchor. Facing the shaky Cody Bradford, **Zack Gelof** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill advantage and a 10% park boost, making him a \"Strong\" start that should be leveraged for maximum value. He is joined in the top tier by **Brendan Donovan** (64.97) and **Lawrence Butler** (62.28); **Brendan Donovan** benefits from a 14% platoon edge against Hunter Brown, while **Lawrence Butler** capitalizes on the same favorable park and SP skill matchup as **Zack Gelof**, effectively neutralizing the inherent risk of a platoon disadvantage. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (62.55) and **Bryce Harper** (62.13) remain set-and-forget core pieces, providing reliable production even against competent arms like Mize and Kremer.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Gavin Sheets** (52.95) from the active lineup. While his SP skill and platoon splits against Tanner Bibee were promising, he fell just short of the efficiency thresholds maintained by the likes of **Justin Crawford** and **Daulton Varsho**. **Justin Crawford** earns his utility spot despite a lower projection, as we prioritize his speed floor in this specific 5x5 Roto context. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Yainer Diaz** (40.78); he sits right at the bottom of our \"Strong\" tier and represents our highest risk today due to a tough matchup against Bryan Woo and a projected bottom-of-the-order assignment. Owners should monitor official lineups, as any further demotion in the order for **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, or **Jung Hoo Lee** could push these players into \"Marginal\" territory, necessitating a pivot to our bench assets if efficiency scores dip further.",
